Let a frontend with no window show the map info box itself

An app that draws the map as a picture gets the map info box painted into it: text at the profile's display font
that a screen reader cannot read, that moves and scales with the picture while a finger drags it, and that the app
cannot keep clear of its own controls. The box's content was reachable only as pixels.

- TMapPainter::mapInfo() gives what the enabled contributors return for a room, in the box's order;
  paintMapInfo() paints from it, so the GUI's box is unchanged.
- TMapPainter::View::mPaintMapInfo, set by default, leaves the box out of a frame when cleared; PaintResult::mapInfo
  then holds its lines.
- THeadlessSession::setMapInfoPainted(false) has renderMap() and renderAppMap() leave the box out, and mapInfo()
  gives each contributor's text, bold, italic and colour and the box's background for either map. The contributors
  run at each draw as before, so registerMapInfo(), enableMapInfo() and the rest act as they do in the GUI.
- docs/headless.md describes them.

Tested by Mudlet/android's native/tests/test_mudlet_engine.py (map_info: the lines of the built-in and a script's
contributor, their order, style and colour, enabling and disabling one, the box's colour, and the frame's pixels
without the box). The desktop is unchanged.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

